conceptually place for multiple lines.

00:12:02.399 --> 00:12:04.480 line:83%
In this case I'm
dealing with only one item

00:12:04.519 --> 00:12:05.639 line:85%
that's why I have one line.

00:12:07.559 --> 00:12:10.960 line:83%
And I see quantity
which I wanted to pick.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:11.679 line:85%
I needed one.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.480 line:85%
And how many I managed to handle?

00:12:15.919 --> 00:12:16.120 line:85%
Nothing.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:17.200 line:85%
Why?

00:12:17.759 --> 00:12:20.559 line:83%
This information we
can get from the summary part

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:21.639 line:85%
which is added here.

00:12:22.039 --> 00:12:23.720 line:85%
Because pickable quantity is zero.

00:12:24.399 --> 00:12:29.759 line:83%
In the advanced workhouse
with directed put away and pick

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.399 line:83%
the workhouse is
split into different zones

00:12:32.679 --> 00:12:35.480 line:85%
and only one of them contains items

00:12:35.519 --> 00:12:37.159 line:85%
which can be picked for shipment

00:12:37.399 --> 00:12:40.200 position:59% line:85%
or for example for future consumption.

00:12:40.919 --> 00:12:42.120 line:85%
So that's called pickable one.

00:12:42.639 --> 00:12:44.240 line:85%
And how do we calculate them?

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:48.399 position:58% line:83%
You can see that in
general in workhouse I have 10 items.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:51.879 line:83%
I can explore ledger
entries that not super useful

00:12:52.679 --> 00:12:55.039 position:58% line:85%
but I can go and explore bin content.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:58.000 line:83%
It will also show me
how these 10 are distributed.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.440 line:83%
And yes, I have a lot in
my workhouse in different bins.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:07.440 line:83%
Nine of them pieces
are in the pickable bins

00:13:07.879 --> 00:13:12.639 line:83%
but unfortunately it is
either blocked or dedicated.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:17.159 position:56% line:83%
Means it has a very
specific purpose and not for picking

00:13:17.639 --> 00:13:19.720 line:85%
or both and dedicated and blocked.

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:23.360 line:83%
And I also have one
thing, one piece outstanding

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.480 line:85%
in the receive bin.

00:13:26.399 --> 00:13:28.799 line:83%
So it's very easy
for me to get unblocked.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:33.480 line:83%
I need to find the put
away document and process it.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.679 position:56% line:85%
For some reason it was not processed

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:38.320 position:63% line:85%
but at least I know whom to ask for help

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:40.320 line:85%
with getting unblocked.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:44.720 line:83%
Before it was more
complicated to troubleshoot

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:45.720 line:85%
now it is shorter.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.720 position:59% line:85%
What about more complicated scenarios?

00:13:49.279 --> 00:13:50.159 line:85%
Of course I have them.

00:13:50.399 --> 00:13:52.960 line:83%
Let's scroll to the
different workhouse shipment.

00:13:53.399 --> 00:13:56.600 line:83%
It has two items,
different types of items

00:13:56.639 --> 00:13:58.120 line:85%
to demonstrate different scenarios.

00:13:58.799 --> 00:13:59.840 line:85%
Let's click create pick.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.879 line:83%
And I already know that
I would like to show summary.

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:08.639 line:83%
Okay, in this situation
you can see that for the first line

00:14:08.679 --> 00:14:13.519 line:83%
we managed to pick
zero but for the second line

00:14:13.799 --> 00:14:16.159 line:85%
something can be picked.

00:14:16.399 --> 00:14:18.240 position:58% line:85%
But let's take a look at the details.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.120 line:83%
First of all, here
it's interesting to notice

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:23.639 line:83%
that pickable bins,
actually we have something.

00:14:23.679 --> 00:14:28.639 line:83%
If I was drill down I can
get bin content on pickable bins.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:33.519 line:85%
Where dedicated toggle is disabled

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:37.919 line:83%
and there is no
blocking of outbound movements.

00:14:38.279 --> 00:14:42.159 line:83%
So this is very good
bin and it has some quantity

00:14:42.759 --> 00:14:44.559 position:56% line:85%
which theoretically could be picked.

00:14:45.519 --> 00:14:46.480 line:85%
But, but.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.679 line:85%
This item has item tracking.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:51.200 position:58% line:85%
If I scroll down I can see that yeah,

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.759 position:56% line:85%
this item has item tracking defined.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:58.120 line:83%
And this specific item
has serial number information card

00:14:58.559 --> 00:15:02.279 line:85%
with blocked field enabled.

00:15:02.879 --> 00:15:05.519 line:83%
So basically I cannot use
this item because it's blocked.

00:15:05.919 --> 00:15:07.960 line:83%
And I get this
information again right here.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:09.960 line:85%
So I just need to find this item,

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.120 line:85%
figure it out why it is blocked,

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:16.799 line:83%
maybe unblock it if
necessary and also unblock myself.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.559 line:85%
Let's take a look at the next line.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.039 line:85%
This is more complicated scenario

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:24.159 line:83%
because now it
has, it involves reservation

00:15:24.519 --> 00:15:26.120 line:85%
and reservation has some impact.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:27.840 line:85%
So what do we want?

00:15:27.879 --> 00:15:29.399 line:85%
We want to pick four.

00:15:31.039 --> 00:15:33.759 position:58% line:85%
And how many do we have in warehouse?

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:35.039 line:85%
Four.

00:15:35.559 --> 00:15:37.000 line:85%
So kind of like what's the problem?

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:37.679 line:85%
Yeah.

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:42.480 line:83%
The problem is that
there are some other orders

00:15:42.519 --> 00:15:46.159 position:58% line:83%
which also needs to be
picked, shipped, consumed, et cetera.

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:47.639 line:85%
And they have a high priority.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:48.200 line:85%
Why?

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:49.879 line:85%
Because they are reserved.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:51.559 line:85%
So this one is not reserved.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.080 position:64% line:85%
So it has no less priorities than others.

00:15:55.279 --> 00:15:58.000 line:83%
So in this case,
we should not make orders

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:59.879 position:61% line:85%
with high priority, which are reserved.

00:16:01.799 --> 00:16:04.399 position:63% line:85%
Should not make them impossible to ship.

00:16:04.879 --> 00:16:07.279 position:59% line:83%
It's okay to make it
difficult to ship, but not impossible.

00:16:07.919 --> 00:16:08.720 line:85%
Let me explain.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:13.399 line:83%
So while we have a
total quantity in warehouse 10,

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.639 line:85%
four are impeccable bins,

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:19.519 position:63% line:85%
which can be picked, shipped right away.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.759 position:56% line:85%
But we also have six somewhere else.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:26.399 line:85%
Where do we have them?

00:16:28.679 --> 00:16:31.240 position:56% line:83%
We have four
impeccable bins, as we already know,

00:16:31.279 --> 00:16:33.840 position:64% line:85%
but we also have four in the putaway bin.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.320 line:85%
So it's like a different storage,

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.840 position:58% line:85%
which requires movement if necessary.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:42.759 line:83%
So we consider this
quantity to be something

00:16:44.519 --> 00:16:46.639 line:83%
which we need to
compare with reservations.

00:16:47.679 --> 00:16:50.720 position:56% line:85%
So eight is potentially can be used.

00:16:50.759 --> 00:16:52.840 line:83%
Yeah, it requires
some additional actions.

00:16:52.879 --> 00:16:55.799 line:83%
For example, if it's in
putaway, it's in received bins,

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:57.159 line:85%
and you need to process putaway.

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:58.960 line:85%
If it's in bulk storage bin,

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.480 position:61% line:85%
you need to move it into pickable bins,

00:17:01.519 --> 00:17:02.840 line:85%
but it can be done.

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:06.920 line:85%
That's why it is okay to take stuff

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.920 line:83%
from the pickable
bin for some other bins,

00:17:09.319 --> 00:17:12.039 line:83%
unless we still have
something in the warehouse

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:14.240 line:85%
which can be shipped for reserve.

00:17:15.319 --> 00:17:17.039 position:56% line:85%
So what about reservation situation?

00:17:17.559 --> 00:17:18.799 line:85%
Yeah, we reserved eight.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:21.079 position:63% line:85%
Eight, we reserved for this sales order,

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:25.839 line:83%
which sounds like,
okay, then 100% is reserved.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.519 line:85%
Not really, not really.

00:17:28.839 --> 00:17:30.359 line:85%
Because out of this eight reserved,

00:17:30.519 --> 00:17:31.799 line:85%
we already picked.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.880 line:83%
So it means this stuff is
already moved to the shipping bin.

00:17:37.039 --> 00:17:41.559 line:85%
And so it can be deducted.

00:17:41.799 --> 00:17:43.960 position:61% line:85%
So out of this eight, we can deduct two

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.720 position:63% line:85%
which are already prepared for shipping.

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:49.240 position:56% line:85%
It's not that trivial, I understand.

00:17:50.039 --> 00:17:50.440 line:85%
Stay with me.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:54.759 line:83%
But we have also two
tips which try to explain

00:17:54.839 --> 00:17:56.440 line:85%
how the stuff is calculated.

00:17:56.839 --> 00:17:59.519 line:83%
So for example, let's
go to the last one, impact.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:03.519 position:58% line:85%
And here we explain that potentially,

00:18:04.079 --> 00:18:05.599 line:85%
shipable from warehouse is eight.

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:07.400 line:83%
It's like
everything which is in warehouse

00:18:07.559 --> 00:18:09.200 line:85%
except in the shipment bin,

00:18:09.599 --> 00:18:11.119 position:59% line:85%
because shipment bin or dedicated bin,

00:18:11.559 --> 00:18:15.279 line:83%
which is already
almost loaded to the truck.

00:18:15.319 --> 00:18:16.319 line:85%
So forget about them.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:19.440 line:83%
But potentially,
shipable eight, okay, here.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.160 line:85%
But we also have reservation,

00:18:22.079 --> 00:18:24.279 line:83%
except reservations
which are already shipped.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:26.839 line:83%
So reservation,
then we compare these two.

00:18:27.599 --> 00:18:30.839 line:85%
And this delta is what we can take

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:34.200 line:85%
for other non-reserved orders.

00:18:34.599 --> 00:18:36.039 line:85%
So in this case, the delta is two.

00:18:36.519 --> 00:18:38.400 line:83%
So that's why we're
adjusting pickable quantity

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:39.640 line:85%
from four to two.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:43.519 position:56% line:85%
And this is how quantity is defined.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:48.640 line:83%
I have the same text
written for in the release node.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:50.400 line:83%
And we're also, of
course, updating the documentation.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.319 line:85%
Probably with more fancy schemas.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.680 position:61% line:85%
All right, so in this case, I have two.

00:18:58.119 --> 00:19:00.039 position:61% line:85%
So system already created pick for two.

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.119 line:85%
How can I get unblocked

00:19:03.359 --> 00:19:05.240 line:83%
if I really, really
need to pick this stuff?

00:19:05.279 --> 00:19:06.400 line:85%
So I have two options.

00:19:06.799 --> 00:19:08.519 line:85%
I either reserve this sales order,

00:19:08.559 --> 00:19:10.119 line:85%
then reserve against reserve.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.200 position:56% line:85%
There is no prioritization conflict.

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:14.799 position:59% line:85%
So this one can be processed directly.

00:19:15.119 --> 00:19:17.119 position:56% line:85%
Or I will go and cancel reservation.

00:19:19.559 --> 00:19:22.519 position:63% line:85%
Because I decided that it is okay to do.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:26.799 line:83%
We will buy more stuff
later for this specific order.

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:28.000 line:85%
It is okay.

00:19:28.039 --> 00:19:29.359 line:85%
We explored, we met from.

00:19:30.079 --> 00:19:34.960 line:83%
Now I can close this
window and run create pick again.

00:19:35.839 --> 00:19:36.839 line:85%
Let's activate it again.

00:19:38.039 --> 00:19:40.079 line:83%
For the second round,
you can see that the first line

00:19:40.119 --> 00:19:41.920 line:83%
still nothing
changed because we still blocked.

00:19:42.559 --> 00:19:44.079 line:85%
And we didn't take any action.

00:19:44.119 --> 00:19:48.839 line:83%
But the second line, we
had two remaining to be picked.

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:50.160 line:85%
And they can be picked.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:51.640 line:85%
So all good with this line.

00:19:53.079 --> 00:19:56.480 line:83%
So what we figured
it out in this demonstration

00:19:56.839 --> 00:20:01.720 line:83%
that first of all, now you
do not need to use directed pick

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.119 line:85%
if the customer or user requires

00:20:04.599 --> 00:20:06.279 line:85%
some workhouse capabilities.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:08.480 line:85%
First of all, you can implement it

00:20:09.079 --> 00:20:11.519 position:61% line:85%
for different departments individually.

00:20:12.279 --> 00:20:14.400 line:83%
Like, okay, let's
start with a shipping team

00:20:14.599 --> 00:20:15.839 line:85%
because they are most ready

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.279 line:83%
and do not touch
manufacturing or jobs, et cetera.

00:20:20.599 --> 00:20:22.279 line:85%
Or you can use different policies.

00:20:22.319 --> 00:20:23.559 position:61% line:85%
For example, here we're using shipping,

00:20:23.799 --> 00:20:25.640 position:59% line:85%
here we're inventory picks, et cetera.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:27.400 position:58% line:85%
And different combinations, all good.

00:20:28.039 --> 00:20:31.400 line:83%
And also, even if
we're using the basic workhouse,

00:20:32.039 --> 00:20:34.079 line:83%
we still can benefit
from advanced capabilities

00:20:34.319 --> 00:20:37.400 line:83%
like put away
templates, picking by ranking,

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:42.160 line:83%
and also allow or do
not allow creation of lines

00:20:42.839 --> 00:20:44.160 line:85%
in pick and put away documents

00:20:44.279 --> 00:20:45.799 line:85%
if there are some problems.

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.119 line:85%
Means we allow or do not allow

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:50.759 position:61% line:85%
workhouse employee or workhouse manager

00:20:50.799 --> 00:20:52.319 line:85%
to solve problems by themselves.

00:20:52.599 --> 00:20:53.920 line:85%
So giving them some control.

00:20:55.279 --> 00:20:58.799 line:83%
Also, we have an ability
to receive more than ordered,

00:20:59.359 --> 00:21:01.200 line:85%
also using inventory put away

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:04.559 line:83%
together with direct
update of purchase document

00:21:04.759 --> 00:21:05.559 line:85%
or workhouse receipt.

00:21:06.279 --> 00:21:09.960 line:83%
This unblocks you and
doesn't impact your decision

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.680 line:85%
about which process you need to use

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:14.599 line:83%
because all of
them supporting overreceive.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:18.839 line:83%
And if you decided
to use directed put away

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:19.960 line:85%
and pick warehouses,

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:22.720 line:83%
now you need to
spend dramatically less time

00:21:22.759 --> 00:21:25.200 position:64% line:85%
analyzing the nothing to handle situation

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:27.519 line:85%
because you can get more insights

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.920 position:61% line:85%
from the special troubleshooting window

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:35.680 position:61% line:85%
which gives you all details right away.

00:21:36.839 --> 00:21:39.400 line:83%
So if you're
interested in workhouse session,

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.400 line:83%
probably you're also
interested in another technology

00:21:42.599 --> 00:21:44.240 position:63% line:85%
like it's barcode scanning capabilities.

